      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-14T01:38:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "atomic_set() and atomic_read() aren\u0027t really providing any value here other than guaranteeing that a compiler can\u0027t read/write it using multiple accesses (eg, writing as 4 separate bytes and reading back as word). You can do this by making this an unsigned int and using:\n\n  foo \u003d READ_ONCE(freqs-\u003elast_index);\n\nand\n\n  WRITE_ONCE(freqs-\u003elast_index, foo);",
      "parentUuid": "0741add8_201913c1",
      "revId": "6f13fe4149cf156862dcdbe83078b07fd70895c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "047980e1_4b180f65",
        "filename": "drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_times.c",
